+## Staged updates
+
+`update` transfers, activates, health-checks, and confirms in one run. When the
+transfer window and the reboot window are hours apart, split it in two:
+
+```sh
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+# ... later, when a reboot is safe ...
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+`stage` validates policy, erases and programs the inactive slot, and has the
+device verify the image digest. It never selects the candidate slot and never
+reboots, so the device carries on running confirmed firmware. The result is
+written to the staging journal (`staging_file`), one record per device, newest
+replacing older.
+
+`activate` finishes from that record alone; the package is not needed again. The
+record is consumed whatever the outcome. If the device stopped matching its
+record — different product, running version, rollback counter, held transfer, or
+accepted byte count — activation stops with `staged_update_lost` before boot
+state moves, and the image must be staged again. Activating a device with no
+record fails with `nothing_staged`.
+
 Every command accepts `--json`; progress remains on standard error so standard
 output is a single machine-readable record. `--quiet` suppresses successful human
 output, while `--verbose` reports configuration and connection detail.
 
